### Selected Items (4)

1. **ProteinDock: A physics-informed layer to improve protein-protein docking reliability** — bioRxiv 10.64898/2026.07.17.739238 (Kimmel lab, Ohio State, posted 2026-07-20, abstract-only — body still rendering). Physics-informed layer composed with Rosetta pushes CAPRI Acceptable from 47.4% → 80.2% on Docking Benchmark 5.5. Truncated form also re-ranks outputs from deep-learning docking tools (AF3, Boltz, Chai). Dominant pick: direct antibody-antigen relevance + unusually large reported improvement + practical re-ranker utility.

2. **MolT5-Linker: A Transformer-Based Sequence- and Putative Site-Guided Generative Framework for Antibody-Drug Conjugate Linkers** — J Chem Inf Model, 10.1021/acs.jcim.6c01342 (Wu group, Shanghai Inst Tech, 2026-07-19). Generative model for ADC linker design conditioned on antibody sequence + payload structure. Graph attention network infers attachment sites. Validity 0.90, recovery 0.58, uniqueness 0.54. No wet-lab validation, but proof-of-concept for site-conditioned generation.

3. **Ensembles of in silico structures enable T cell peptide-MHC binding prediction** — bioRxiv 10.64898/2026.07.14.738340 (Greenbaum lab, MSKCC, posted 2026-07-20). Tool: enFoldX. AlphaFold 3 ensemble + biophysical interface features for TCR-pMHC cognate classification at single-amino-acid resolution. Generalizes to unseen peptides, MHCs, TCRs. General template (ensemble+interface-biophysics) likely transfers to antibody-antigen.

4. **ProteinSketch translates spatial intuition into protein design with bimanual interaction in VR** — bioRxiv 10.64898/2026.07.19.739460 (KAIST, posted 2026-07-20). Bimanual VR interface for sketching backbone paths and volumetric envelopes, translated into RFdiffusion constraints. Volumetric conditioning enables high-fidelity anisometric shape control. Cryo-EM validated. Used to extend pre-existing minibinders to previously inaccessible surfaces.

### Excluded Spurious Matches

- `chai`, `esm`, `agent` keyword hits in unrelated biological contexts (e.g., Chai enzyme family, ESM genes)
- CAFE (Head-Gordon lab, Boltz-2 for allosteric fragment screening) — kinase/small-molecule, not antibody-adjacent
- ProtSyntax (protein LLM for post-translational modifications) — not antibody-specific

