- Already shipped today (excluded): BepiPocket + DiscoPocket (Chai-1 restraints, Nielsen, Protein Sci indexed 2026-08-03); LF3DRoPE (Soochow, arXiv 2026-08-02); Seed-guided RFdiffusion for RelE binders (Keating lab, bioRxiv 10.64898/2026.08.02.742339).
- bioRxiv scanned 2026-08-03 and 2026-08-04: 473 total, 63 keyword-matched, 32 antibody/PLM/ML-specific after refining; all sources reachable, no failures.
- arXiv daily cache (500 entries, 2026-07-31 to 2026-08-04): only LF3DRoPE (already shipped) and TransNRank (2026-08-03, neoantigen ranking transformer) were on-brief; TransNRank dropped as weaker fit than the bioRxiv picks.
- PubMed reldate=5, 100 hits, filtered to antibody+ML: CLSS (contrastive PLM sequence+structure, PNAS 2026-08-03) was the strongest candidate but PNAS auth-walled from this host; dropped in favor of full-text-available bioRxiv picks.
- Shortlist after excluding shipped items (all bioRxiv 2026-08-04):
  - Kukulu — JEPA + conditional diffusion for CDR loop reconstruction (Ford, UNC Charlotte + Silico Biosciences) — 10.64898/2026.08.03.742168 **[picked]**
  - CKEA humanized anti-PD-1 antibody generation (Batista lab, Yale) — 10.64898/2026.08.03.742579 **[picked]**
  - SynCodonLM directed evolution in codon space (Cramer lab + Boehringer Ingelheim) — 10.64898/2026.08.03.742557 **[picked]**
  - MAXWELL PLM stability calibration (Hong/Yu, bioinformatics) — 10.64898/2026.07.29.741631 (dropped: no wet-lab, less antibody-tight)
  - Interpreting PLMs / HA-sites for functional regions (Altman lab, Stanford) — 10.64898/2026.07.29.741641 (dropped: methodological/interpretability, less on-brief than the three picks)
  - Humanized anti-ADAMTS13 (Saito et al., biochemistry) — no ML content, dropped
  - ValidaTe TCR-mimic (immunology) — TCR-mimic rather than antibody-side, dropped
- Full-text depth: Kukulu (7-page PDF, full text via r.jina.ai); CKEA (22-page PDF, full text); SynCodonLM (39-page PDF, full text). All three had abstract-only bioRxiv HTML at first fetch (posted this morning); the PDF route via r.jina.ai recovered full text for all three. No auth-walled sources.
